 "* weightless coins": "",
 "* weightless coins. Items go out most valuable first, each to whoever has the least so far.": "",
 "A hoard is a chest actor in the Hoards folder of the Actors sidebar, opened on D35E's loot sheet. Place its token on a scene and the players can loot it.\nThis tab builds and edits hoards. If you have none yet, press New Hoard first: the rest of the tour points at a hoard's parts.": "",
 "A hoard is a chest actor in the Hoards folder that players can loot from its token. Make one with New Hoard, then fill it here.": "",
 "A hoard's loot sheet has a Hoard Editor button in its title bar that opens this tab on that hoard.": "",
 "A trap for the chest: any trap actor in the world (Axecleft's Traps, Poisons, and Diseases makes them for every SRD trap). It is saved with the hoard.": "",
 "Add items by hand": "",
 "After a fight, sweep the fallen into the hoard and share it out from here. It takes the Treasure Generator's token loot and the coins it rolled from the selected tokens, or, with none selected, from every creature on the scene that is defeated, dead or at 0 hp.\nTick Everything they carry to take their own gear and coins as well. You see what moves before it does.": "",
 "After a fight: takes the token loot (and the coins it rolled) from the selected tokens, or, with none selected, from every fallen creature on the scene (defeated, dead or at 0 hp). Ticked, it takes all their gear and coins too. You see what moves first.": "",
